   "risk_level": "low",
   "notes": "Owning a Flipper Zero is legal in the US, the UK and the EU. What can get you in trouble is USE, not ownership: transmitting on sub-GHz frequencies you are not licensed for, opening a gate or car that is not yours, cloning an access credential without permission, or interfering with a radio service are separate offences almost everywhere, and they are the offences people actually get charged with. Treat this as 'check your own local law', not legal advice. Specific to this board: it adds no transmit capability of any kind, so it raises none of the radio-law questions the Flipper itself does."
