   "notes": "Owning a Flipper Zero is legal in the US, the UK and the EU. What can get you in trouble is USE, not ownership: transmitting on sub-GHz frequencies you are not licensed for, opening a gate or car that is not yours, cloning an access credential without permission, or interfering with a radio service are separate offences almost everywhere, and they are the offences people actually get charged with. Treat this as 'check your own local law', not legal advice. Specific to this board: sending deauthentication frames against networks you do not own or have written authorisation to test is illegal in most jurisdictions - in the US the FCC has issued multi-million-dollar fines to hotels and venues for Wi-Fi deauth, entirely separately from computer-misuse law."
