   "notes": "This is the highest-risk item in this batch. Owning it is fine. Transmitting is where the trouble is: in the US, 433 MHz unlicensed use falls under 47 CFR 15.231, which permits only short control transmissions at low field strength and explicitly forbids continuous transmission - a 100 mW amplified carrier is not compliant, and 433.05-434.79 MHz also sits inside the 70 cm amateur allocation where you need a licence. In the EU, 433.05-434.79 MHz is a short-range-device band with a 10 mW ERP limit for most sub-bands, so 100 mW is illegal there too without a specific authorisation. Amplified transmission also converts what might be nuisance-level interference into something regulators actually chase. Check your local rules and do not transmit into the air without authorisation."
